title: 'rpc_server: set `TCP_NODELAY` on JSON-RPC connections'
doc:
- audience: Node Dev
  description: |-
    ### Summary
    The JSON-RPC server never sets `TCP_NODELAY`, so [Nagle's algorithm](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nagle%27s_algorithm) stays enabled on every RPC socket. jsonrpsee sets the option in its own accept loop and defaults it to on, but that loop never runs: substrate accepts connections itself and hands jsonrpsee an already-accepted socket.

    CI runtime for `revive-differential-tests` rose to ~2 hours after the subxt 0.50 bump moved eth-rpc onto `chainHead`; the main cause is the latency between the messages a `chainHead` call sends.

    ### Change
    Set `TCP_NODELAY` on every accepted connection, restoring jsonrpsee's default for all nodes. Messages that would otherwise be coalesced are now sent separately, which can increase the number of emitted TCP packets.
crates:
- name: sc-rpc-server
  bump: patch
